  HF.addChapter({
    id: 'revenue-leases',
    part: 'p4',
    title: 'Revenue Recognition & Leases',
    subtitle: 'IFRS 15, IFRS 16 and the time value of money',
    art: 'handshake',
    level: 'Advanced',
    minutes: 35,
    quote: 'Revenue is the single most important number investors look at. That’s why it has its own five-step rulebook.',
    goals: ['Apply the IFRS 15 / ASC 606 five-step model', 'Handle bundles, variable consideration and principal-vs-agent', 'Use present value in accounting', 'Account for leases as a lessee under IFRS 16 (and know how ASC 842 differs)'],
    blocks: [
      { t: 'h', text: 'The five-step model' },
      { t: 'steps', items: [{ t: 'Identify the contract', d: 'An enforceable agreement with commercial substance, approved, with identifiable rights and payment terms, and probable collection.' }, { t: 'Identify performance obligations', d: 'Each distinct promise: a good or service the customer can benefit from on its own and that’s separately identifiable.' }, { t: 'Determine the transaction price', d: 'Fixed amounts plus <b>variable consideration</b> (discounts, rebates, bonuses — constrained so a big reversal is unlikely), adjusted for significant financing components and non-cash consideration.' }, { t: 'Allocate the price', d: 'In proportion to <b>stand-alone selling prices</b> (SSP).' }, { t: 'Recognise revenue', d: 'When (point in time) or as (over time) each obligation is satisfied — i.e., when control transfers.' }] },
      { t: 'widget', name: 'revrec' },
      { t: 'h3', text: 'Over time or at a point in time?' },
      { t: 'p', html: 'Revenue is recognised <b>over time</b> if any of these is true: (1) the customer receives and consumes the benefit as you perform (cleaning, subscriptions), (2) you create/enhance an asset the customer controls (building on their land), or (3) the asset has no alternative use to you <i>and</i> you have an enforceable right to payment for work done so far. Otherwise, at the <b>point in time</b> control transfers (indicators: legal title, physical possession, risks & rewards, acceptance, right to payment).' },
      { t: 'cards', cols: 3, items: [{ icon: '🎟️', t: 'Principal vs agent', d: 'Do you control the good before it goes to the customer? Principal → gross revenue. Agent (marketplace, travel agent) → only your commission.', color: 'blue' }, { icon: '🎁', t: 'Loyalty points & warranties', d: 'Points = separate obligation (defer part of the price). Assurance warranties = provision; extended/service warranties = separate obligation.', color: 'yellow' }, { icon: '📄', t: 'Contract balances', d: '<b>Contract asset</b>: performed but right to payment is conditional. <b>Receivable</b>: unconditional. <b>Contract liability</b>: paid before performing.', color: 'green' }] },
      { t: 'pencil', items: [{ q: 'Max sells a bike ($900 SSP) with a free 1-year service plan ($100 SSP) for $950. How much revenue on day 1?', input: true, a: 'Allocate $950 by SSP: bike 900/1,000 × 950 = <b>$855</b> on delivery; service $95 recognised over 12 months (~$7.92/month).' }] },

      { t: 'h', text: 'Time value of money (you’ll need it)' },
      { t: 'formula', html: 'PV = FV ÷ (1 + r)ⁿ', note: 'Present value of a future amount. Annuity PV = payment × [1 − (1 + r)⁻ⁿ] ÷ r' },
      { t: 'widget', name: 'tvm' },
      { t: 'p', html: 'Discounting shows up all over modern accounting: leases, long-term provisions (e.g., decommissioning), bonds, impairment (value in use), pensions and significant financing components in revenue.' },

      { t: 'h', text: 'Leases under IFRS 16 (lessee)' },
      { t: 'p', html: 'Before 2019 many leases were “off balance sheet”. Now a lessee recognises nearly all leases on the balance sheet:' },
      { t: 'list', items: ['<b>Lease liability</b> = PV of future lease payments, discounted at the rate implicit in the lease (or the incremental borrowing rate).', '<b>Right-of-use (ROU) asset</b> = lease liability + initial direct costs + prepayments + restoration costs − incentives.', 'Then: depreciate the ROU asset (usually straight-line) and unwind interest on the liability (effective interest).', 'Exemptions: short-term leases (≤12 months) and low-value assets (e.g., laptops) can be expensed straight-line.'] },
      { t: 'p', html: '<b>Example:</b> Max leases a shop for 3 years, $10,000 per year paid at the end of each year, incremental borrowing rate 5%. PV = 10,000 × 2.7232 = <b>$27,232</b>.' },
      { t: 'entry', title: 'Commencement', lines: [['Right-of-use Asset', 27232, 0], ['Lease Liability', 0, 27232]] },
      {
        t: 'table',
        caption: 'Lease liability schedule',
        head: ['Year', 'Opening', 'Interest 5%', 'Payment', 'Closing'],
        rows: [
          ['1', '27,232', '1,362', '(10,000)', '18,594'],
          ['2', '18,594', '930', '(10,000)', '9,524'],
          ['3', '9,524', '476', '(10,000)', '0'],
        ],
      },
      { t: 'entry', title: 'Year 1', lines: [['Interest Expense', 1362, 0], ['Lease Liability', 8638, 0], ['Bank', 0, 10000]] },
      { t: 'entry', lines: [['Depreciation — ROU Asset', 9077, 0], ['Accumulated Depreciation — ROU', 0, 9077]], narr: '27,232 ÷ 3 years' },
      { t: 'p', html: 'Year 1 P&L charge: 1,362 + 9,077 = <b>$10,439</b> — more than the $10,000 cash paid. Lease expense is <b>front-loaded</b> under IFRS 16. EBITDA rises (rent is gone from operating expenses), and lease principal payments move to <b>financing</b> cash flows.' },
      { t: 'compare', cols: [{ t: 'IFRS 16 (lessee)', color: 'blue', items: ['Single model: all leases → depreciation + interest', 'Front-loaded expense'] }, { t: 'US GAAP ASC 842 (lessee)', color: 'yellow', items: ['Also on balance sheet, but two types', '<b>Finance leases</b>: like IFRS 16', '<b>Operating leases</b>: single straight-line lease cost in operating expenses'] }] },
      { t: 'odoo', html: 'Odoo handles revenue timing through <b>deferred revenue</b> on invoice lines (start/end dates), <b>subscriptions</b> (recurring invoicing) and down payments/milestones on sales orders. IFRS 16 lease schedules are typically set up as an <b>asset</b> (ROU) with its depreciation board plus a manual/loan-style schedule for the liability — or via a localization/add-on.' },
      { t: 'bullets', items: ['Five steps: contract → obligations → price → allocate → recognise.', 'Allocate by stand-alone selling prices.', 'Over time vs point in time depends on control transfer criteria.', 'Principal reports gross revenue; agent reports net commission.', 'IFRS 16: lease liability = PV of payments; ROU asset depreciated; interest unwound.', 'ASC 842 keeps an operating-lease straight-line expense pattern.'] },
    ],
    quiz: [
      { q: 'Step 4 of IFRS 15 allocates the transaction price based on…', o: ['Cost of each item', 'Stand-alone selling prices', 'Equal shares', 'Cash received'], a: 1, e: 'Relative SSP allocation.' },
      { q: 'An online marketplace that never controls the goods should report…', o: ['Gross sales value', 'Only its commission', 'Nothing', 'Cost of sales'], a: 1, e: 'It is an agent.' },
      { q: 'Cash received before performance is a…', o: ['Contract asset', 'Contract liability', 'Receivable', 'Revenue'], a: 1, e: 'You owe performance.' },
      { q: 'PV of $1,000 in 2 years at 10%?', o: ['$826', '$1,210', '$800', '$909'], a: 0, e: '1,000 ÷ 1.21 = 826.' },
      { q: 'Under IFRS 16, the lease liability is initially measured at…', o: ['Total undiscounted payments', 'PV of lease payments', 'Fair value of the building', 'Zero'], a: 1, e: 'Discounted lease payments.' },
      { q: 'Compared with straight-line rent, IFRS 16 expense in early years is…', o: ['Lower', 'Higher (front-loaded)', 'Identical', 'Zero'], a: 1, e: 'Interest is highest early on.' },
      { q: 'Which lease can be expensed straight-line under IFRS 16?', o: ['10-year building lease', '6-month equipment rental', 'Aircraft lease', 'Any lease above $1m'], a: 1, e: 'Short-term (≤12 months) exemption.' },
    ],
    cards: [
      ['IFRS 15 five steps', 'Contract, performance obligations, transaction price, allocation, recognition.'],
      ['Performance obligation', 'A distinct promise to transfer a good or service.'],
      ['Stand-alone selling price', 'Price at which an item would be sold separately.'],
      ['Contract liability', 'Obligation to transfer goods/services for which consideration was received.'],
      ['Right-of-use asset', 'Lessee’s asset representing the right to use a leased item.'],
      ['Lease liability', 'PV of unpaid lease payments.'],
      ['Present value', 'Future amount discounted: FV ÷ (1 + r)ⁿ.'],
    ],
  });

